# UX workflow: Step Edit contextual back from child content.
# Purpose: verifies LEFT_CENTER backs out of a child Step Editor to the parent
# Step Editor context instead of closing straight back to the step grid.

0 scenario sequencer
50 capture screen sequencer_ready

# Enable root step 1, open Step Edit, and enter its micro-sequence child.
150 tap MACRO_1 60
350 capture screen root_step_enabled
450 button MACRO_1 down
1500 tick
1550 capture screen root_step_edit_open
1600 button MACRO_1 up
1700 encoder NAV 1
1780 encoder NAV 1
1860 encoder NAV 1
1940 encoder NAV 1
2020 encoder NAV 1
2100 encoder NAV 1
2180 encoder NAV 1
2260 capture screen root_micro_row_focused
2360 tap NAV 60
2660 capture screen micro_context_open

# Edit the first child step, then back to the parent Step Editor.
2760 button MACRO_1 down
3820 tick
3880 capture screen child_step_edit_open
3940 button MACRO_1 up
4060 encoder NAV 1
4140 encoder NAV 1
4220 encoder OPT 0.65
4360 capture screen child_step_note_edited
4460 tap LEFT_CENTER 60
4760 capture screen returned_to_parent_step_edit

# At the parent Step Editor root, LEFT_TOP closes back to the step grid.
4860 tap LEFT_TOP 60
5100 capture screen parent_step_edit_closed
